    tags: ["work"],
    raw: "LED-418: the monthly reconciliation takes 52 min and peaks at 11 GB RAM, and the pod got OOM-killed once last month. finally profiled it.\n\ncProfile + py-spy on a one-week sample (~700k rows, 38 min on my laptop): 61% of wall time in pandas merge, because the join keys are object dtype (strings like 'NGP-00012345'), 22% in an iterrows loop that applies carrier surcharges row by row, and the rest is reading parquet (all 31 columns although we use 9).\n\nplan, in order of expected win: (1) convert keys to categorical/int32 up front, (2) replace the iterrows loop with a merge on carrier+service, (3) usecols for parquet. dont touch the schedule. nothing done today other than measure, but i know what to do tomorrow and that's a good feeling",
    cleaned: "LED-418: the monthly reconciliation takes 52 minutes and peaks at 11 GB of RAM, and the pod got OOM-killed once last month. I finally profiled it.\n\ncProfile and py-spy on a one-week sample (about 700,000 rows, 38 minutes on my laptop) show 61% of wall time in the pandas merge, because the join keys are object dtype (strings like NGP-00012345), 22% in an iterrows loop that applies carrier surcharges row by row, and the rest reading Parquet (all 31 columns although we use 9).\n\nThe plan, in order of expected win: (1) convert the keys to categorical or int32 up front, (2) replace the iterrows loop with a merge on carrier and service, (3) read only the needed Parquet columns. Do not touch the schedule. Nothing done today other than measuring, but I know what to do tomorrow, and that is a good feeling.",
