    raw: "found why some Harbor Gate requests hang for 30 s when an upstream stalls. the proxy handler builds the upstream call with context.Background() instead of the incoming ctx, so the client's 2 s deadline never propagates. Go 1.22, one line, the kind of bug that makes you stare at the ceiling. fix in PR #812 + a test with a fake upstream that sleeps 10 s and asserts the client sees DEADLINE_EXCEEDED at ~2 s. renata approved in 10 min. in staging with a stalled upstream p99 went 30 s -> 2 s. grepped the repo for other context.Background() in request paths, found 2 more, filed HG-77. not fixing them tonight",
    cleaned: "Found why some Harbor Gate requests hang for 30 seconds when an upstream stalls. The proxy handler builds the upstream call with context.Background() instead of the incoming context, so the client's 2-second deadline never propagates. Go 1.22, one line, the kind of bug that makes you stare at the ceiling. The fix is in PR #812, with a test that uses a fake upstream sleeping 10 seconds and asserts the client sees DEADLINE_EXCEEDED at about 2 seconds. Renata approved it in 10 minutes. In staging with a stalled upstream, p99 went from 30 s to 2 s.\n\nI grepped the repo for other context.Background() calls in request paths and found two more, which I filed as HG-77. I am not fixing them tonight.",
    summary: "Found that Harbor Gate's proxy handler used context.Background() for upstream calls, so client deadlines were ignored and requests hung up to 30 seconds; PR #812 fixes it, cutting staging p99 under a stalled upstream from 30 s to 2 s. Two more similar spots were filed as HG-77.",
